      <profile id="r18-final-shard-infernal-profile" name="Infernal Phoenix" hidden="false" typeId="prof-ranged" typeName="Ranged Weapon"><characteristics><characteristic name="Range" typeId="ranged-range">24"</characteristic><characteristic name="S" typeId="ranged-s">8</characteristic><characteristic name="AP" typeId="ranged-ap">1</characteristic><characteristic name="Type" typeId="ranged-type">Witchfire, Beam, Melta</characteristic></characteristics></profile></profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule name="Source Entry" id="r41-unit-xv-12-magnus-shard-of-the-crimson-king-source" hidden="true">
          <description>A Fragment of the Crimson King
Magnus was shattered long before his final damnation was complete. Fragments of his soul were scattered throughout the Warp and across the material realm, each possessing only a portion of the Crimson King’s impossible power. Such a shard is less a creature than a psychic apparition — a thought given form, flickering between reality and unreality. Bullets pass through it, shells are cast aside by distortions in space and only weapons touched by the Warp can reliably harm it. Yet the manifestation is unstable, and the same psychic energies which empower it may at any moment tear it from reality entirely.
Magnus, Shard of the Crimson King | 7 | 7 | 7 | \ | 7\ | 6 | 5 | 10 | –
Force Organisation:
• Lord of War
Unit Composition:
• 1 Magnus, Shard of the Crimson King
Unit Type:
• Monstrous Creature (Character)
Wargear:
• Aetheric Blade
Special Rules:
• Fear
• Fearless
• Master of the Legion
• Psyker (Mastery Level 5\)
• Ethereal
• Incorporeal Will
• The Crimson King Unbound
• Beyond the Prosperine Cults
• Nothing to Bless
• Master of the Great Ocean
• Beyond the Perils of the Warp
• The Warp Breathes
• The Crimson King Shattered
RESTRICTIONS
Magnus, Shard of the Crimson King may only be selected for a Thousand Sons army. An army may not include both Magnus, Shard of the Crimson King and Magnus in his mortal form.
AETHERIC BLADE The Aetheric Blade is a Master-crafted Force Weapon. Magnus resolves attacks made with it at Strength 7. ETHEREAL Magnus is not truly a physical creature, but a fragment of psychic consciousness temporarily given form. Magnus possesses seven Wounds, but has no conventional Toughness characteristic and receives no Armour or Invulnerable Save. Shooting Non-psychic shooting attacks may only hit Magnus on an unmodified roll of 6. A successful hit may only wound Magnus on an unmodified roll of 6. Weapons which normally hit automatically still require a 6 to wound Magnus. Magnus receives no save against successful Wounds. Blast Weapons Non-psychic Blast weapons cannot directly strike Magnus. If Magnus would be beneath the template after scatter has been resolved, move the template directly away from Magnus by the minimum distance required for him to no longer be beneath it. Other models may still be hit normally. Close Combat Attack Type To Wound Normal close-combat weapon 6+ Power Weapon, Power Fist, Thunder Hammer or equivalent 5+ Force Weapon 2+ Magnus receives no save against successful Wounds. If a Force Weapon inflicts one or more Wounds upon Magnus, its wielder may attempt to activate the weapon normally. If successful, each Wound inflicted by that Force Weapon becomes a Massive Wound and inflicts D3 Wounds. Psychic Attacks Psychic shooting attacks and Wounds caused directly by psychic powers ignore the normal shooting restrictions of Ethereal. Whenever such an effect requires Magnus to possess a Toughness characteristic, treat him as Toughness 7 for that effect only. Magnus receives no save against resulting Wounds. Instant Death and Massive Wounds Magnus is immune to Instant Death. Massive Wounds affect Magnus normally only when caused by an activated Force Weapon or by a psychic effect which specifically inflicts Massive Wounds. Otherwise, an attack which would cause Instant Death or a Massive Wound simply inflicts one Wound. INCORPOREAL WILL Magnus may never declare a charge or make a Pursuit move. He may fight normally if charged and may Consolidate normally after combat. Magnus may never join another unit and no model may join him. THE CRIMSON KING UNBOUND Magnus is a Mastery Level 5 Psyker. Before deployment, choose six psychic powers for Magnus from any combination of the following disciplines: • Biomancy
• Divination
• Pyromancy
• Telekinesis
• Telepathy Magnus also always knows the following two unique powers: • Infernal Phoenix
• Strands of Fate These two powers do not count towards his six selected powers. Magnus may attempt to invoke up to five psychic powers during each player turn, specifically overriding the normal ProHammer maximum for Psykers.Magnus may successfully manifest each individual psychic power no more than once during the same player turn. Magnus may invoke up to two Witchfire powers during the same Shooting phase. INFERNAL PHOENIX Type: Witchfire, Beam Range S AP Special 24" 8 1 Melta Resolve Infernal Phoenix using the normal rules for a Beam psychic power. STRANDS OF FATE Type: Malediction
Range: 18" Choose one enemy non-Vehicle unit within range and line of sight. Until the beginning of Magnus’ next turn, the affected unit must pass a Leadership Test each time it wishes to: • Move
• Shoot
• Charge If the test is failed, that action is lost for that phase. BEYOND THE PROSPERINE CULTS Magnus is not assigned to a Prosperine Cult and gains no Cult Arcana or Cult Mastery benefit. He counts as belonging to the Thousand Sons for army selection and rules which refer to friendly Thousand Sons models. NOTHING TO BLESS Magnus may never be the target of a Blessing, whether manifested by himself or another Psyker. Any Blessing manifested by Magnus must target another eligible friendly unit. MASTER OF THE GREAT OCEAN Magnus ignores all Leadership penalties caused by Disturbance in the Warp. In addition, psychic powers successfully invoked by Magnus do not count when determining Disturbance in the Warp penalties for other Psykers. Magnus remains subject to all other rules concerning Psychic Tests and Perils of the Warp. Magnus may attempt to Deny the Witch against any psychic power if either the Psyker invoking the power or its target is within 24" of Magnus. Resolve the Deny the Witch attempt normally using Magnus' own Mastery Level. Each psychic power may still only be the subject of one Deny the Witch attempt, as normal. BEYOND THE PERILS OF THE WARP Whenever Magnus would suffer Perils of the Warp, ignore the normal Perils result. Magnus suffers no Wound or other effect. Instead, place one Instability Counter beside him. Each Instability Counter imposes a cumulative –1 modifier on Magnus’ next Warp Breath roll. After that Warp Breath roll has been resolved, remove all Instability Counters. There is no maximum number of Instability Counters. THE WARP BREATHES At the beginning of each Thousand Sons turn in which Magnus is on the battlefield, roll a D6 and apply any modifiers from Instability Counters. Modified Result Effect 1 or less The Crimson King Fades 2–5 Reality Holds 6+ The Warp Ascendant THE CRIMSON KING FADES Magnus immediately disappears from the battlefield and is placed in Reserve. He is not destroyed. Beginning on the following Thousand Sons turn, roll normally for Magnus to return from Reserve. When Magnus returns, he enters play using Deep Strike and scatters normally. Magnus may use psychic powers during the turn in which he returns. If Magnus remains in Reserve when the battle ends, he counts as destroyed for Victory Point purposes. This does not trigger The Crimson King Shattered. REALITY HOLDS No additional effect occurs. THE WARP ASCENDANT Until the beginning of the next Thousand Sons turn, every Psyker on the battlefield, friendly or enemy, may re-roll failed Psychic Tests. However, any Psychic Test containing a double causes Perils of the Warp, even if the Psychic Test succeeds. A double which is subsequently re-rolled still causes Perils. Magnus converts any Perils he suffers into Instability Counters as normal. THE CRIMSON KING SHATTERED If Magnus loses his final Wound and is actually destroyed, the psychic backlash tears through the minds of his sons. Immediately, every friendly non-Vehicle unit with Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) suffers: D3 Strength 4 AP– hits. Then every friendly Thousand Sons Psyker or Brotherhood of Psykers suffers Perils of the Warp. A Thousand Sons Independent Character with the Psyker rule suffers Perils twice instead, resolving each result separately. These effects ignore range and line of sight. For the purposes of Signs and Portents, all Perils caused by The Crimson King Shattered count as one single triggering event. Apply Signs and Portents once after all resulting Perils and casualties have been resolved. |</description>
        </rule>
      <rule id="r18-final-shard-blade" name="Aetheric Blade" hidden="false"><description>Master-crafted Force Weapon. Magnus resolves attacks made with it at Strength 7.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-ethereal" name="Ethereal" hidden="false"><description>Magnus has seven Wounds but no conventional Toughness and no Armour or Invulnerable Save. Non-psychic shooting hits only on an unmodified 6 and successful hits wound only on an unmodified 6; automatic-hit weapons still need a 6 to wound. Non-psychic Blast weapons cannot directly strike him and are moved the minimum distance away after scatter. In close combat, normal weapons wound on 6+, Power Weapons/Power Fists/Thunder Hammers or equivalent on 5+, and Force Weapons on 2+. Psychic attacks ignore the normal shooting restrictions and treat him as Toughness 7 only when a Toughness value is required. He is immune to Instant Death; Massive Wounds affect him normally only from an activated Force Weapon or a psychic effect which specifically inflicts Massive Wounds, otherwise such effects inflict one Wound.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-will" name="Incorporeal Will" hidden="false"><description>Magnus may never declare a charge or make a Pursuit move. He may fight normally if charged and Consolidate normally after combat. Magnus may never join another unit and no model may join him.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-unbound" name="The Crimson King Unbound" hidden="false"><description>Magnus is a Mastery Level 5 Psyker. Before deployment choose six powers from Biomancy, Divination, Pyromancy, Telekinesis and Telepathy. He also always knows Infernal Phoenix and Strands of Fate; these do not count toward the six selected powers. He may invoke up to five powers per player turn, may successfully manifest each individual power no more than once in that player turn, and may invoke up to two Witchfire powers in the same Shooting phase.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-infernal" name="Infernal Phoenix" hidden="false"><description>Witchfire — Beam. Resolve using the normal rules for a Beam psychic power.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-strands" name="Strands of Fate" hidden="false"><description>Malediction, 18 inches. Choose one enemy non-Vehicle unit in range and line of sight. Until the beginning of Magnus’ next turn, the affected unit must pass a Leadership Test each time it wishes to Move, Shoot or Charge; a failed test loses that action for the phase.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-cults" name="Beyond the Prosperine Cults" hidden="false"><description>Magnus is not assigned to a Prosperine Cult and gains no Cult Arcana or Cult Mastery benefit. He counts as Thousand Sons for army selection and rules referring to friendly Thousand Sons models.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-blessing" name="Nothing to Bless" hidden="false"><description>Magnus may never be the target of a Blessing, whether manifested by himself or another Psyker. Any Blessing manifested by Magnus must target another eligible friendly unit.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-ocean" name="Master of the Great Ocean" hidden="false"><description>Magnus ignores Leadership penalties from Disturbance in the Warp. Powers successfully invoked by Magnus do not count when determining Disturbance penalties for other Psykers. He may attempt to Deny the Witch if either the invoking Psyker or the target is within 24 inches, using his own Mastery Level; each power may still only be the subject of one Deny attempt.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-perils" name="Beyond the Perils of the Warp" hidden="false"><description>Whenever Magnus would suffer Perils of the Warp, ignore the normal result and place one Instability Counter beside him instead. Each counter imposes a cumulative -1 on his next Warp Breath roll; remove all Instability Counters after that roll. There is no maximum number of counters.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-breathes" name="The Warp Breathes" hidden="false"><description>At the beginning of each Thousand Sons turn while Magnus is on the battlefield, roll D6 and apply Instability Counter modifiers. 1 or less: The Crimson King Fades — Magnus enters Reserve without being destroyed and, from the following Thousand Sons turn, returns by normal Reserve roll using Deep Strike; if still in Reserve at battle end he counts as destroyed for Victory Points. 2–5: Reality Holds — no additional effect. 6+: The Warp Ascendant — until the next Thousand Sons turn every Psyker may re-roll failed Psychic Tests, but any Psychic Test containing a double causes Perils even if successful and even if that double is subsequently re-rolled. Magnus converts his Perils into Instability Counters normally.</description></rule><rule id="r18-final-shard-shattered" name="The Crimson King Shattered" hidden="false"><description>If Magnus actually loses his final Wound and is destroyed, every friendly non-Vehicle unit with Legiones Astartes (Thousand Sons) immediately suffers D3 Strength 4 AP– hits. Then every friendly Thousand Sons Psyker or Brotherhood suffers Perils of the Warp; a Thousand Sons Independent Character with Psyker suffers Perils twice. These effects ignore range and line of sight. For Signs and Portents, all Perils caused by this rule count as one triggering event, applied after all resulting Perils and casualties are resolved.</description></rule></rules>
